From: Anze <aanzdev@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] GuiMenu: launchGame window/input discipline for blocking GUI launchers

The PERF CONTROL entries (System Settings > Performance and the Quick
Access modal) and the STEAMLIKE THEME MANAGER entry launch full-screen
Pyxel GUIs through a bare Utils::Platform::runSystemCommand() on the UI
thread. That blocks ES in waitpid() with SDL completely unpumped - unlike
game/Tools launches, which go through FileData::launchGame and wrap the
blocking child in window->deinit()/init() (closing and REOPENING every
SDL joystick) plus window->normalizeNextUpdate().

Why that matters (root cause of the "OLED screensaver in Perf Control
wedge", diagnosed live on device 2026-07-03): every suspend/wake runs the
Odin 3 sleep quirk that restarts InputPlumber (rsinput geni workaround),
which deletes and recreates the virtual "Microsoft X-Box One Elite 2 pad"
evdev node. If that happens while ES is blocked inside one of these bare
launchers, ES keeps reading the DELETED node forever (verified:
/proc/<es>/fd -> "/dev/input/event7 (deleted)") and comes back deaf to
all gamepad input. 60 s later (ScreenSaverTime) the "oled" screensaver
fires, and since no button press can ever reach ES, nothing dismisses it:
screen shows the sweeping OLED band, SSH works, controls dead, reboot
required. In ES proper the same IP restart is harmless because SDL is
pumping udev hotplug events live - which is exactly why the wedge was
only ever seen "inside an app".

The deltaTime jump on resume (mTimeSinceLastInput += whole blocked
duration) could also trip the screensaver instantly at app exit;
normalizeNextUpdate() clamps it exactly like launchGame does.

Fix: give the three blocking GUI launchers the proven launchGame
discipline - window->deinit() before, window->init() +
window->normalizeNextUpdate() after. init() re-enumerates SDL joysticks
from scratch, so whatever happened to input devices while ES was blocked,
it comes back with fresh fds. Sub-second command entries (charge-mode,
gamepad-profile set, governors, ...) stay bare: ES is only blocked for
milliseconds there, no suspend/wake can slip in.

Signed-off-by: Anze <aanzdev@gmail.com>
---
--- a/es-app/src/guis/GuiMenu.cpp
+++ b/es-app/src/guis/GuiMenu.cpp
@@ -2037,9 +2037,21 @@
 	// Shown only where the tool is installed (the SM8xxx handhelds that bundle
 	// the Pyxel venv). The launcher takes over the screen and is killable by the
 	// global panic combo; ES resumes when it exits.
+	// Blocking full-screen launcher: same window/input discipline as
+	// FileData::launchGame. deinit/init re-opens every SDL joystick on return,
+	// so ES survives an InputPlumber restart that happened while it was blocked
+	// (every suspend/wake restarts IP and recreates the virtual pad node; a bare
+	// runSystemCommand leaves ES reading a deleted evdev node = deaf controls,
+	// and 60s later the OLED screensaver fires with nothing able to dismiss it).
+	// normalizeNextUpdate() keeps the resumed frame's multi-minute deltaTime
+	// from instantly tripping the screensaver idle timer on exit.
 	if (Utils::FileSystem::exists("/usr/share/perfcontrol/perfcontrol-gui")) {
-		s->addEntry(_("PERF CONTROL"), false, [] {
+		s->addEntry(_("PERF CONTROL"), false, [this] {
+			Window* w = mWindow;
+			w->deinit();
 			Utils::Platform::runSystemCommand("\"/usr/share/perfcontrol/perfcontrol-gui\"", "", nullptr);
+			w->init();
+			w->normalizeNextUpdate();
 		});
 	}
 
@@ -4906,8 +4918,15 @@
 	// runs full-screen (the launcher restarts ES on exit if anything changed).
 	if (Settings::getInstance()->getString("ThemeSet") == "steamlike")
 	{
-		s->addEntry(_("STEAMLIKE THEME MANAGER"), true, [] {
+		// Blocking full-screen launcher: launchGame discipline (see the PERF
+		// CONTROL entry in openSystemSettings) so ES re-opens its joysticks on
+		// return. If the launcher restarts ES the init() never runs - harmless.
+		s->addEntry(_("STEAMLIKE THEME MANAGER"), true, [this] {
+			Window* w = mWindow;
+			w->deinit();
 			Utils::Platform::runSystemCommand("/usr/bin/steamlike-theme-manager", "", nullptr);
+			w->init();
+			w->normalizeNextUpdate();
 		});
 	}
 
@@ -5741,8 +5760,13 @@
 		// without diving into System Settings > Performance. Each is gated on the
 		// same condition as its System Settings counterpart.
 		if (Utils::FileSystem::exists("/usr/share/perfcontrol/perfcontrol-gui")) {
-			s->addEntry(_("PERF CONTROL"), false, [] {
+			// Blocking full-screen launcher: launchGame discipline (see the
+			// System Settings entry) so ES re-opens its joysticks on return.
+			s->addEntry(_("PERF CONTROL"), false, [window] {
+				window->deinit();
 				Utils::Platform::runSystemCommand("\"/usr/share/perfcontrol/perfcontrol-gui\"", "", nullptr);
+				window->init();
+				window->normalizeNextUpdate();
 			});
 		}
 		// Charging mode: full charge / battery care (~80%) / bypass (run on AC).
